WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.889 --> 00:00:04.810
For all the blood-pumping brawls, sentimental
scenes, and general doom and gloom seen on

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:09.480
screen in Avengers: Infinity War, there was
just as much laughter, banter, and goofs that

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.150
played out behind the scenes.

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:15.030
And thanks to the Blu-ray release of Infinity
War, which features a two minute-long gag

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:19.789
reel, viewers at home can witness the best
of those bloopers in one handy spot.

00:00:19.789 --> 00:00:21.509
Something wrong with Wong

00:00:21.509 --> 00:00:25.699
After Bruce Banner crash-lands at the New
York Sanctum following his cosmic face-off

00:00:25.699 --> 00:00:28.949
with Thanos, he meets up with Iron Man, Wong,
and Doctor Strange.

00:00:28.949 --> 00:00:33.410
Wong and Doctor Strange give a crash course
on the Infinity Stones, Bruce explains just

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:38.460
how wicked Thanos is, and Iron Man goes to
call Captain America for help, hoping to reconcile

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:40.829
after their falling out in Captain America:
Civil War.

00:00:40.829 --> 00:00:45.199
But when Iron Man notices that the wind has
picked up, the four men slowly turn to face

00:00:45.199 --> 00:00:49.340
the Sanctum's streetside door and realize
that Thanos' lieutenants have already touched

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:50.640
down on Earth.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:52.399
Pretty dramatic stuff, right?

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:56.920
Well, during filming, actor Benedict Wong
couldn't really keep it that way.

00:00:56.920 --> 00:01:04.909
[Dramatic music]

00:01:04.909 --> 00:01:07.159
Bumbling Benedict and Mush-Mouth Mark

00:01:07.159 --> 00:01:11.440
They may be two of the smartest characters
in the entire Marvel Cinematic Universe, but

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:15.490
for a few minutes during filming Avengers:
Infinity War, Doctor Strange and Bruce Banner

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:17.939
definitely acted like a couple of doofuses.

00:01:17.939 --> 00:01:21.970
When Bruce and Doctor Strange emerge from
a portal and greet Iron Man and Pepper Potts

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:26.360
in the park, actors Benedict Cumberbatch and
Mark Ruffalo seem to forget how to, like,

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:27.360
talk and stuff.

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:31.000
"I'm Doctor, ugh, I'm Doctor I can't walk."

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:34.560
[Incoherent stammering]

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.130
Falcon gets funny

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:40.450
Anthony Mackie's Falcon wasn't as major a
player in Avengers: Infinity War as some of

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:41.450
the other superheroes.

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:45.850
But a lack of narrative influence doesn't
equate to a lack of quality bloopers.

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:50.070
During the battle in Wakanda, Falcon soars
through the sky to take down the Black Order

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:51.290
and the Outriders.

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:55.130
Between takes, Mackie made sure to paint a
great mental picture for everyone of what

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:57.640
his scene would look like when the movie was
finished:

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:00.140
"Flying about 80 miles an hour.

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:02.369
Just a big chocolate missile."

00:02:02.369 --> 00:02:06.439
When shooting another portion of the Wakanda
battle, Mackie had another important acting

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:09.280
moment, this time with co-director Joe Russo.

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:11.950
"Hey Russo, you want me to go Jamie Foxx on
this one?"

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:13.680
"No I want Denzel."

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:14.680
"Oh, s---.

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:18.020
Everybody put on your sunglasses, Denzel's
coming out."

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:22.319
And that wasn't the only time Mackie discussed
his acting process between takes.

00:02:22.319 --> 00:02:26.740
During the film's intense final sequence,
Falcon rests slumped on the Wakandan forest

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:27.740
floor.

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:29.160
It's a heartbreaking moment for viewers.

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:34.040
Turns out it's because Mackie was channelling
his Infinity War co-star Don "War Machine"

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:35.040
Cheadle for inspiration:

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:38.060
"I'm going full Cheadle on this take.

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:40.320
Full Cheadle."

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:42.790
Black Panther vs. the Bleating Goats

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:47.530
Poised yet passionate, and undeniably powerful,
Chadwick Boseman's T'Challa, better known

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:52.269
as Black Panther, is generally able to keep
his cool under even the worst of situations.

00:02:52.269 --> 00:02:56.849
This rings especially true in Infinity War,
when Black Panther gifts Sebastian Stan's

00:02:56.849 --> 00:03:01.269
war-weathered Bucky Barnes a new bionic arm
and subtly asks him to join the resistance

00:03:01.269 --> 00:03:05.530
against Thanos, whose Black Order was minutes
away from landing in Wakanda.

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:11.080
"This one may be tired of war, but the White
Wolf has rested long enough."

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:15.379
Upon seeing his upgrade, Bucky and Black Panther
have a simple, dramatic exchange:

00:03:15.379 --> 00:03:17.670
"Where's the fight?"

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:19.960
"On its way."

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:25.129
The blooper reel features an extended version
of this moment which is...less dramatic.

00:03:25.129 --> 00:03:26.129
The problem?

00:03:26.129 --> 00:03:31.120
A couple of extras just couldn't keep quiet
during filming specifically, two chatty goats.

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:33.790
"I know you have found something.

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:36.520
A sense of peace."

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:38.530
[Loud goat noises]

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:41.330
"OK, now you are going too far!"

00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:42.970
A hairy situation

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:47.500
Nearing the third act of the film, Black Widow,
Bruce Banner, Captain America, Scarlet Witch,

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:51.810
Falcon, War Machine, and Vision all travel
to Wakanda to visit Shuri, the genius younger

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:56.239
sister of T'Challa, who's known for her advanced
technological creations like the latest version

00:03:56.239 --> 00:03:57.520
of the Black Panther suit.

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:01.720
The group hopes that Shuri can safely and
successfully remove the Mind Stone from Vision's

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:05.551
forehead and that they can destroy it before
Thanos seizes it and uses it to power the

00:04:05.551 --> 00:04:09.730
Infinity Gauntlet, snap his fingers, and kill
half the universe.

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:14.370
Once in the lush, futuristic country, the
heroes wind up preparing to battle the purple-muscled

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:18.790
despot, with Black Widow joining the fight
inside a ship alongside Wakandan warriors

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:20.800
and members of the Dora Milaje .

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:25.100
Like so many scenes throughout the film, this
sequence was shot in front of a green screen,

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:29.880
but also required the use of a machine to
simulate real wind whipping past and the machine

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:34.530
kinda worked a little too well, both in this
scene and in one starring the Elizabeth Olsen

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:37.010
as the Scarlet Witch from earlier in the film.

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:39.240
"Because you're worth it!"

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:45.000
If they ever gets tired of acting, Johansson,
Olsen, and the rest of the Infinity War cast

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:47.480
could totally do shampoo commercials instead.

